findings.description:
The mirror rule (light X% ↔ dark (100−X)%) is typed by hand at over 100 sites in this diff. Five of the changed sites already break it, which suggests the rule is too easy to get wrong by hand. A helper beside `dark-light-choose` would encode it once:

```scss
@function dark-light-mirror($lightness) {
  @return dark-light-choose(scale-color($primary, $lightness: $lightness), scale-color($secondary, $lightness: 100% - $lightness));
}
```

Converting the sites to this helper would have prevented the four mis-pairings above.
